    "text": "Ezechiel se witega l\u00e6r\u00f0 Godes bydelas \u00fe\u00e6t hi beorgan heom silfum wi\u00f0 Godes yrre.\nHe cw\u00e6\u00f0 Godes wordum \u00feus to heom eallum: Hec dicit Dominus: Audiens ex ore meo sermonem\nCy\u00f0 swi\u00f0e georne, he cw\u00e6\u00f0, Godes word wide \u00fee of Gode silfum \u00e6ror asprungon, & gif \u00feu sinfullan\nAnd wa \u00feam hirdum, he cw\u00e6\u00f0, \u00fee esta\u00f0 heom silfum swa heom betst lica\u00f0 & godcundre heorde ne\nGehyra\u00f0 git, hirdas, Godes word georne: nu ic silf wille, he cw\u00e6\u00f0, on his dome witan \u00e6t \u00feam hirdum\nAnd wa \u00feam hirdum, he cw\u00e6\u00f0, \u00fee freta\u00f0 & forswelga\u00f0 folces sinna; \u00f0\u00e6t syndon \u00fea gifran & \u00fea heom\nEalswa Issaias se witega hwilum be \u00feam spr\u00e6c: Canes muti non ualentes latrare.\nEalswilce he cw\u00e6de \u00fe\u00e6t gemidlede hundas ne beorca\u00f0 to nahte.\nDumbe beo\u00f0 \u00fea bydelas & to f\u00e6ste gemidlede \u00fee for ege o\u00f0\u00f0e lufe o\u00f0\u00f0e \u00e6nigre worldscame eargia\u00f0 &\nAnd wace beo\u00f0 \u00f0a hirdas funden to heorde \u00fee nella\u00f0 \u00fea heorda \u00fee hi healdan sculon, huru mid clipunge\nNis nan swa yfel sca\u00f0a swa is deofol silf; he bi\u00f0 a ymbe \u00fe\u00e6t an, hu he on manna sawlum m\u00e6st\n\u00d0onne motan \u00fea hyrdas beon swi\u00f0e wacole & geornlice clipigende \u00fee wi\u00f0 \u00feone \u00feeodsca\u00f0an folc sculon\nAnd se \u00fee oferhogige \u00fe\u00e6t he heom ne hliste, h\u00e6bbe he him gem\u00e6ne \u00fe\u00e6t wi\u00f0 god silfne.\nSit nomen Domini benedictum ex hoc nunc et usque in seculum.",
